From: Lumo Assistant <proton.me>
Date: 30 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu6-isys: Increase line alignment from 64 to 256 bytes

The xe kernel driver (iGPU and dGPU) requires 4096-byte stride alignment
for DMA-BUF texture imports via eglCreateImageKHR. The IPU6 ISYS driver
allocates buffers with line_align=64, producing 3904-byte stride
(ALIGN 3864 to 64 = 3904). Changing to line_align=256 produces 4096-byte
stride (ALIGN 3864 to 256 = 4096), enabling zero-copy DMA-BUF import.

This fixes eglCreateImageKHR failures when using GPU-accelerated SoftISP
with Intel Arc dGPU or Iris Xe iGPU on Alder Lake-P systems.


Signed-off-by: Aleksei <alksbrs@proton.me>

--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
@@ -241,7 +241,7 @@
 	else
 		*bytesperline = DIV_ROUND_UP(*width * pfmt->bpp, BITS_PER_BYTE);
 
-	*bytesperline = ALIGN(*bytesperline, 64);
+	*bytesperline = ALIGN(*bytesperline, 256);
 
 	/*
 	 * (height + 1) * bytesperline due to a hardware issue: the DMA unit
